{
  "title": "Greetings, sounds and courtesy",
  "note": "Every German noun is capitalized. W sounds like English v, ß sounds like ss, and ä, ö, ü are separate vowels. Use du with friends, family and children; use Sie, always capitalized, with adults you don't know well.",
  "src": { "t": "Deutsch im Blick, Kapitel 1: Begrüßungen", "u": "https://coerll.utexas.edu/dib/voc.php?k=1&s=1" },
